    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the late 19th century West City was a small settlement adjoining Benton on the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_City%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early 20th century saw Polish, Lithuanian, and English immigrants work in local coal mines.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_City%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During Prohibition, West City became notorious for bootlegging and gambling, with Birger and Shelton gangs vying for control.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_City%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The last public hanging in Illinois occurred in West City when Birger was executed in 1928.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_City%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Despite its rough past, West City established its first church, Prospect, in 1921, later becoming First Baptist.",
